1
00:00:00,801 --> 00:00:04,238
Hon, I'm glad
Dex got out of the hospital already.

2
00:00:04,238 --> 00:00:07,207
I'm so happy to finally see you.

3
00:00:07,207 --> 00:00:09,810
Hey! Why are you hugging my wife?

4
00:00:10,678 --> 00:00:12,468
Who are you?

5
00:00:14,081 --> 00:00:15,716
That's our house!

6
00:00:15,716 --> 00:00:16,784
Why are you in our house?

7
00:00:16,784 --> 00:00:17,918
- Where's my wife?
- Punch him!

8
00:00:17,918 --> 00:00:18,886
Where's Joyce?

9
00:00:18,886 --> 00:00:21,374
Where's Dex? What's going on?

10
00:00:22,454 --> 00:00:24,780
Maybe you need to sober up first.

11
00:00:26,327 --> 00:00:28,896
Get him inside until he sobers up.

12
00:00:28,896 --> 00:00:31,198
Wait, wait... Sir! Sir! Sir!

13
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:33,027
Kid, you can come out now.

14
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,939
Liam, son.

15
00:00:42,509 --> 00:00:46,102
There wasn't a day
that I didn't wish to be with you.

16
00:00:47,214 --> 00:00:48,349
<i>I will wake up.</i>

17
00:00:48,349 --> 00:00:51,418
<i>I will wake up.
I will wake up from this nightmare!</i>

18
00:00:51,418 --> 00:00:53,253
What the...

19
00:00:53,921 --> 00:00:55,805
Hello, Love.

20
00:01:09,803 --> 00:01:12,235
We met seven years ago.

21
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:19,600
On a bridge near the bus stop
in a province far from Manila.

22
00:01:19,601 --> 00:01:23,384
It was that fateful day when...

23
00:01:23,384 --> 00:01:25,775
I thought I was all alone.

24
00:01:26,647 --> 00:01:30,421
Then you came into my life.

25
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:37,093
Then from then on, we became inseparable.

26
00:01:42,069 --> 00:01:45,802
When was it again?

27
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:54,757
March 22, 2015.

28
00:01:56,483 --> 00:01:58,419
<i>At a bus stop?</i>

29
00:01:58,419 --> 00:02:01,388
<i>In a province far from Manila?</i>

30
00:02:01,388 --> 00:02:04,158
<i>So instead of following Joyce that day,</i>

31
00:02:04,158 --> 00:02:08,296
<i>I stayed inside the bus
and reached the last bus stop.</i>

32
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:12,436
<i>And that's where I met this woman?</i>

33
00:02:22,990 --> 00:02:25,712
Is no one else getting off?

34
00:02:25,712 --> 00:02:29,083
Next stop, Segunda!

35
00:02:29,083 --> 00:02:30,651
Get in.

36
00:02:30,651 --> 00:02:32,519
Is there anyone else going to Segunda?

37
00:02:32,519 --> 00:02:34,118
Boss.

38
00:02:41,767 --> 00:02:45,632
[Segunda Bus Stop]

39
00:02:45,632 --> 00:02:48,501
Make sure everyone gets off.

40
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:13,260
That's why...

41
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:19,250
every March 22, we celebrate our meetsary.

42
00:03:22,269 --> 00:03:27,707
It matters to us more than our anniversary.

43
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:32,771
Because you changed my life...

44
00:03:35,482 --> 00:03:37,976
by just being there for me.

45
00:03:45,926 --> 00:03:47,530
Liam.

46
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,799
I want you to know...

47
00:03:52,799 --> 00:03:55,624
I'm willing to do that to you, too.

48
00:04:01,441 --> 00:04:08,374
I am here for you
whatever you are going through.

49
00:04:09,883 --> 00:04:12,444
You can tell me anything.

50
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:16,882
I'll be the last person to judge you.

51
00:04:34,618 --> 00:04:37,487
I don't understand what's happening.

52
00:04:38,406 --> 00:04:43,277
I only tried to write down
everything that was on my mind.

53
00:04:43,951 --> 00:04:48,977
I wished for my life to change.

54
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:54,394
I wished I wasn't the reason

55
00:04:54,394 --> 00:04:58,131
for my wife and son's miserable life.

56
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:00,601
Then it was like magic...

57
00:05:00,601 --> 00:05:04,995
When I woke up, I was here.

58
00:05:06,106 --> 00:05:09,176
It was like a different world.

59
00:05:09,176 --> 00:05:10,410
<i>It's like this.</i>

60
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:12,379
<i>Same world, same universe.</i>

61
00:05:12,379 --> 00:05:17,117
But here, there are lots of new people.

62
00:05:17,117 --> 00:05:22,522
<i>I found out I was working
for my father's construction company.</i>

63
00:05:22,522 --> 00:05:24,391
<i>I became wealthy.</i>

64
00:05:24,391 --> 00:05:26,630
<i>I was able to pay for my mom's treatment.</i>

65
00:05:27,527 --> 00:05:30,216
And the plot twist here...

66
00:05:31,265 --> 00:05:33,497
is that Joyce isn't part of my life.

67
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:39,840
<i>I didn't marry the woman
I was supposed to marry.</i>

68
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,309
But the ultimate plot twist is...

69
00:05:42,309 --> 00:05:46,113
I met a different girl named Via.

70
00:05:46,113 --> 00:05:48,081
They say she's my girlfriend.

71
00:05:48,081 --> 00:05:51,269
She's not my wife yet.
We don't have a child...

72
00:05:53,116 --> 00:05:55,112
We don't have a child together.

73
00:05:56,490 --> 00:05:58,992
<i>My son disappeared. Dex disappeared.</i>

74
00:05:58,992 --> 00:06:03,397
Well, in this dream of yours, Liam,

75
00:06:03,397 --> 00:06:06,069
how will you describe what you felt,

76
00:06:06,069 --> 00:06:10,270
realizing all the changes after you woke up?

77
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:13,144
Were you sad or happy?

78
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:16,643
It's not just a single emotion.

79
00:06:16,643 --> 00:06:21,581
It's like I felt every emotion
all at the same time.

80
00:06:21,581 --> 00:06:26,219
Confusion, sadness, happiness, excitement...

81
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:28,055
I felt it all at once, but...

82
00:06:28,055 --> 00:06:32,596
But what's dominant is the question...

83
00:06:33,994 --> 00:06:36,530
How could I do this?

84
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:41,435
How could I wish for it?

85
00:06:41,435 --> 00:06:43,363
So there's guilt?

86
00:06:45,372 --> 00:06:53,146
Maybe because there are wishes we only regret
once it comes true.

87
00:06:53,146 --> 00:06:56,383
Well, it's a good thing
that everything's just a dream.

88
00:06:56,383 --> 00:06:59,052
What I gather from your dream

89
00:06:59,052 --> 00:07:01,922
is maybe you're having a midlife crisis.

90
00:07:01,922 --> 00:07:06,259
You're having a hard time
appreciating the things you have.

91
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:09,363
Maybe you're looking for something new.

92
00:07:09,363 --> 00:07:13,310
Maybe it's time for you
to develop a new career or a hobby,

93
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:17,401
like learning a foreign language,
or playing an instrument?

94
00:07:18,271 --> 00:07:21,575
A change of career, perhaps.

95
00:07:24,478 --> 00:07:26,413
Doc... Doc, sorry. Sorry.

96
00:07:26,413 --> 00:07:29,549
Sir Liam, isn't your session done yet?

97
00:07:29,549 --> 00:07:31,618
Sir Danilo has been calling me.

98
00:07:31,618 --> 00:07:33,518
He's looking for you.

99
00:07:51,071 --> 00:07:52,105
- One moment, Sir...
- What?

100
00:07:52,105 --> 00:07:53,974
Let me fix your collar.

101
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:56,410
You're so formal.

102
00:07:56,410 --> 00:07:58,678
Sorry, Sir, come again?

103
00:07:58,678 --> 00:08:00,814
You're too formal with me.

104
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:04,017
This formal attire I'm wearing is enough.

105
00:08:04,017 --> 00:08:06,294
You've been like that since the other day.

106
00:08:07,254 --> 00:08:09,521
Good morning, Sir William Herrera.

107
00:08:13,174 --> 00:08:15,800
And stop calling me "Sir".

108
00:08:15,801 --> 00:08:16,833
Just call me Liam.

109
00:08:16,834 --> 00:08:19,033
Good morning, Sir William!
[Casa Fuerte Properties]

110
00:08:19,033 --> 00:08:20,901
I can't do that, Sir.

111
00:08:20,901 --> 00:08:23,837
I don't want to lose my job.

112
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:27,073
You will lose your job
if you continue calling me "Sir".

113
00:08:27,073 --> 00:08:28,141
I will fire you.

114
00:08:28,141 --> 00:08:30,316
Please, don't do that, Si...

115
00:08:31,933 --> 00:08:33,713
B-Boss Bro.

116
00:08:33,713 --> 00:08:34,567
I'll just call you that.

117
00:08:34,567 --> 00:08:39,553
I'm not going to fire you,
but Boss Bro is better.

118
00:08:39,553 --> 00:08:42,698
Okay, as you wish, Boss Bro.

119
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:46,960
- Borj?
- What?

120
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:49,829
You've been working for me for years, right?

121
00:08:50,497 --> 00:08:55,068
Six years and nine months to be exact.

122
00:08:55,068 --> 00:08:56,270
Six years and nine months.

123
00:08:56,270 --> 00:09:00,741
So that means you're already loyal to me?

124
00:09:00,741 --> 00:09:03,777
I'm starting to get hurt
by your questions, Boss Bro.

125
00:09:03,777 --> 00:09:05,345
I'm just checking.

126
00:09:05,345 --> 00:09:08,633
I just want to ask for your opinion.

127
00:09:08,634 --> 00:09:10,117
I talked to the psychiatrist.

128
00:09:10,117 --> 00:09:11,867
She told me

129
00:09:11,868 --> 00:09:14,911
maybe I needed a significant change
in my life.

130
00:09:15,722 --> 00:09:20,866
Borj, if you're allowed
to go back to the past

131
00:09:20,866 --> 00:09:24,534
to change or alter your life,

132
00:09:24,534 --> 00:09:26,766
will you do it?

133
00:09:26,767 --> 00:09:30,871
Just like in Miss Universe,

134
00:09:30,871 --> 00:09:32,639
I would say no.

135
00:09:32,639 --> 00:09:36,643
I'm standing here in front of you today

136
00:09:36,643 --> 00:09:39,946
because of the things
that happened in my life.

137
00:09:40,781 --> 00:09:43,517
May it be good or bad.

138
00:09:43,517 --> 00:09:49,556
So, I won't change anything in my past.

139
00:09:49,556 --> 00:09:54,566
That's all, and I thank you.

140
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:56,830
Borj, we're not in the Miss Universe pageant.

141
00:09:56,830 --> 00:10:00,099
Of course, I would say yes.

142
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:06,807
There's always a part of our lives
that we regret.

143
00:10:06,807 --> 00:10:11,211
So if I were given a chance
to change it, why not?

144
00:10:11,211 --> 00:10:12,700
Right?

145
00:10:14,081 --> 00:10:20,186
But our decisions will only lead us
to two directions.

146
00:10:21,655 --> 00:10:26,026
It can bring us to the wrong path...

147
00:10:26,026 --> 00:10:28,279
or to the right one.

148
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:41,490
And about the psychiatrist's advice

149
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:43,544
that something might be missing
in your life...

150
00:10:43,544 --> 00:10:46,446
Well, I'll say there's none.

151
00:10:46,446 --> 00:10:49,216
Because you already have everything.

152
00:10:49,216 --> 00:10:53,520
You are the prince of
the Herrera Holdings Corporation,

153
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:55,889
especially here in Casa Fuerte.

154
00:10:55,889 --> 00:10:57,824
Sir Liam!

155
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:59,092
Good morning.

156
00:10:59,092 --> 00:11:00,894
Mister, hold on.

157
00:11:00,894 --> 00:11:03,063
Borj, it's okay. Let him be. What is it?

158
00:11:03,063 --> 00:11:06,600
I've been waiting for you, Sir.

159
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:09,102
Luckily, I'm on duty right now.

160
00:11:09,102 --> 00:11:13,140
Mister, can you make it faster?
We're going to be late.

161
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:15,542
I will just give this food
that my wife cooked.

162
00:11:15,542 --> 00:11:19,345
Sorry if this is the only thing
we can afford.

163
00:11:21,915 --> 00:11:23,550
What's this?

164
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:26,216
That is a little token of appreciation...

165
00:11:26,216 --> 00:11:28,055
for the help you've given us.

166
00:11:28,055 --> 00:11:29,456
If it wasn't for you,

167
00:11:29,456 --> 00:11:32,358
our youngest child wouldn't
get the treatment.

168
00:11:34,962 --> 00:11:36,763
Is that so?

169
00:11:36,763 --> 00:11:38,507
What is this?

170
00:11:40,902 --> 00:11:42,203
Wow!

171
00:11:42,203 --> 00:11:44,105
It's Ginataang Batute!

172
00:11:44,105 --> 00:11:45,806
This is my favorite.

173
00:11:45,806 --> 00:11:47,275
Thank you so much.

174
00:11:47,275 --> 00:11:48,409
I'm glad to hear that, Sir.

175
00:11:48,409 --> 00:11:50,611
I thought you do not eat food like that.

176
00:11:50,611 --> 00:11:53,014
Thank you so much, Mister.

177
00:11:53,014 --> 00:11:59,287
Please thank your wife,
and also say hi to your child for me.

178
00:11:59,287 --> 00:12:03,858
Sir, we will be forever grateful to you.

179
00:12:03,858 --> 00:12:06,512
Thank you so much, Sir.

180
00:12:07,528 --> 00:12:09,997
I'll get going, Sir.
I'll go back to my duty now.

181
00:12:09,997 --> 00:12:11,566
Thank you so much.

182
00:12:11,566 --> 00:12:12,733
- Thank you so much too.
- Bye, Sir.

183
00:12:12,733 --> 00:12:15,602
I'll get going. Please, excuse me.

184
00:12:17,171 --> 00:12:21,275
Boss Bro, is that delicious?

185
00:12:21,275 --> 00:12:23,644
My mom used to cook this.

186
00:12:23,644 --> 00:12:25,146
Do you want to try it? We can share it.

187
00:12:25,146 --> 00:12:26,914
Okay. I'm already hungry.

188
00:12:26,914 --> 00:12:28,049
Come on, let's try it.

189
00:12:28,049 --> 00:12:29,441
Okay, let's go.

190
00:12:44,531 --> 00:12:46,132
<i>This world is so different.</i>

191
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:47,140
<i>Who would have thought</i>

192
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:50,271
<i>that the man
who used to work himself to the ground</i>

193
00:12:50,271 --> 00:12:53,907
<i>could now help others?</i>

194
00:13:02,116 --> 00:13:03,950
Boss Bro.

195
00:13:06,466 --> 00:13:08,802
What's that? Do I need to read all that?

196
00:13:08,802 --> 00:13:10,491
I've read all of it, Boss Bro.

197
00:13:10,491 --> 00:13:13,593
You already approved everything.
You just need to sign.

198
00:13:13,593 --> 00:13:15,755
I have to sign all of these?

199
00:13:19,232 --> 00:13:20,567
But...

200
00:13:20,567 --> 00:13:23,369
This one needs your approval.

201
00:13:29,730 --> 00:13:32,644
Boss Bro, we don't have time
to go to the mall.

202
00:13:32,644 --> 00:13:34,548
So they just sent these watches over,

203
00:13:34,548 --> 00:13:38,418
since you're a valued customer
of their store.

204
00:13:38,418 --> 00:13:40,386
All you need to do is choose.

205
00:13:49,863 --> 00:13:54,000
Based on your taste,
this looks better, Boss Bro.

206
00:14:19,159 --> 00:14:20,293
Hi, son.

207
00:14:20,293 --> 00:14:22,261
Are you ready?

208
00:14:25,499 --> 00:14:27,400
Ready for what, Dad?

209
00:14:28,602 --> 00:14:32,639
Señor, you call him Señor here in the office.

210
00:14:32,639 --> 00:14:35,875
Ready for what, Señor?

211
00:14:36,977 --> 00:14:40,647
Come on.
Today is the groundbreaking ceremony.

212
00:14:40,647 --> 00:14:44,751
Borj, you did not update your boss
about his schedule.

213
00:14:44,751 --> 00:14:46,853
Sir Liam is ready, Señor.

214
00:14:46,853 --> 00:14:48,988
Just a final touch.

215
00:14:58,865 --> 00:15:01,801
Now he's ready, Señor.

216
00:15:18,485 --> 00:15:20,120
Why are you here?

217
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:22,622
Aren't you busy in Blacksmith?

218
00:15:22,622 --> 00:15:24,558
I have my men there, Dad.

219
00:15:24,558 --> 00:15:26,827
They get paid, okay?

220
00:15:26,827 --> 00:15:31,664
And besides, this is a big day
for my brother, right?

221
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:35,702
Groundbreaking ceremony.

222
00:15:35,702 --> 00:15:40,907
The great Liam has again
surpassed his previous success.

223
00:15:40,907 --> 00:15:45,145
Now, it's the biggest mall in Asia.

224
00:15:45,145 --> 00:15:46,578
Wow!

225
00:15:47,714 --> 00:15:50,516
You really are unstoppable, Bro.

226
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:56,523
I'll go get my boss, VLH.

227
00:15:56,523 --> 00:15:58,525
If he gets injured,

228
00:15:58,525 --> 00:16:00,786
he'll be less good-looking
when he gives his speech.

229
00:16:03,430 --> 00:16:04,982
Speech?

230
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,868
[Grand Pacific Square:
The Biggest Mall in Asia]

231
00:16:15,575 --> 00:16:17,077
Borj...

232
00:16:17,077 --> 00:16:20,180
I didn't know I had to speak.

233
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:24,517
I thought you had it memorized
since last week.

234
00:16:24,517 --> 00:16:26,119
That's how advanced you prepare.

235
00:16:26,119 --> 00:16:27,977
I forgot about it, okay?

236
00:16:27,977 --> 00:16:30,312
We're in trouble.

237
00:16:32,725 --> 00:16:35,679
From being a small construction company,

238
00:16:35,679 --> 00:16:41,233
we have evolved
into a giant development corporation.

239
00:16:41,935 --> 00:16:44,704
All because of this guy over here.

240
00:16:45,872 --> 00:16:53,713
So, it's just right
that he leads our biggest project.

241
00:16:53,713 --> 00:16:57,217
Bigger than the biggest mall
in the continent.

242
00:16:57,217 --> 00:17:01,463
It will be spearheaded by my son.

243
00:17:07,894 --> 00:17:11,986
My son, William Herrera.

244
00:17:35,174 --> 00:17:36,610
Hello.

245
00:17:50,136 --> 00:17:55,141
The biggest mall in the biggest continent.

246
00:17:57,210 --> 00:18:02,014
Lately, I've been bothered
by a huge question.

247
00:18:03,183 --> 00:18:07,920
How prepared am I for this project?

248
00:18:09,789 --> 00:18:11,657
The answer...

249
00:18:12,792 --> 00:18:14,827
It's scary.

250
00:18:17,564 --> 00:18:21,667
The pressure is scary.

251
00:18:23,169 --> 00:18:26,205
It's scary when people go...

252
00:18:31,144 --> 00:18:33,479
when people come.

253
00:18:35,682 --> 00:18:38,384
But what's scarier...

254
00:18:39,319 --> 00:18:45,091
are the things that change our lives.

255
00:18:45,091 --> 00:18:49,995
Things that take us out of our comfort zone.

256
00:18:52,332 --> 00:18:59,338
Things that we can't fully understand
at the beginning.

257
00:19:06,446 --> 00:19:11,217
Just like accepting this project.

258
00:19:11,918 --> 00:19:15,722
It's not just my life that's on the line.

259
00:19:15,722 --> 00:19:25,396
The company and the country's image
are on the line, too.

260
00:19:26,433 --> 00:19:28,701
But I realized...

261
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:33,405
a big change can be worthwhile.

262
00:19:34,074 --> 00:19:38,444
And I just hope I can make you all proud
with this new project.

263
00:19:39,079 --> 00:19:42,449
Because I'm no longer the man
who underestimates himself.

264
00:19:42,449 --> 00:19:45,385
I am sorry to be the bearer of bad news.

265
00:19:45,385 --> 00:19:48,555
But the network has decided
not to proceed with your concept.

266
00:19:48,555 --> 00:19:51,757
And that decision has already been made.

267
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:56,428
I hope you are all proud of me.

268
00:20:30,763 --> 00:20:33,766
Sir William, look here, please.

269
00:20:54,868 --> 00:20:56,322
Liam!

270
00:20:56,322 --> 00:20:58,892
Liam, son!

271
00:20:58,892 --> 00:21:00,059
- Liam!
- Boss Bro.

272
00:21:00,059 --> 00:21:03,630
Yes... your life changed.

273
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:05,498
And we were dragged into it!

274
00:21:05,498 --> 00:21:08,468
You rose to the top...

275
00:21:08,468 --> 00:21:11,371
While we die one by one.

276
00:21:11,371 --> 00:21:14,974
You should die before anyone else!

277
00:21:16,776 --> 00:21:18,044
You monster!

278
00:21:18,044 --> 00:21:19,379
Dad, let's get out of here.

279
00:21:19,379 --> 00:21:21,214
- What?
- He might not be alone.

280
00:21:21,214 --> 00:21:22,612
- Please escort him out.
- Let's go.

281
00:21:22,612 --> 00:21:23,883
- Please secure everything.
- Got it.

282
00:21:23,883 --> 00:21:29,154
You are the reason why we're suffering!

283
00:21:30,056 --> 00:21:31,758
Mister, who are you?

284
00:21:31,758 --> 00:21:33,092
Why do you want to kill me?

285
00:21:33,092 --> 00:21:36,095
Have you forgotten about it?

286
00:21:36,095 --> 00:21:38,565
That's how you rich people are.

287
00:21:38,565 --> 00:21:41,568
You treat poor people like cockroaches

288
00:21:41,568 --> 00:21:46,139
that you can step on and eliminate!

289
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:47,974
Please get him out of here!

290
00:21:47,974 --> 00:21:49,409
Something bad might happen to him.

291
00:21:49,409 --> 00:21:51,578
I'm already old.

292
00:21:51,578 --> 00:21:54,113
I've got nothing to lose.

293
00:21:54,113 --> 00:21:56,649
Until my last breath...

294
00:21:56,649 --> 00:22:01,955
I'll seek justice for what happened to us!

295
00:22:01,955 --> 00:22:03,289
Sir, what happened?

296
00:22:03,289 --> 00:22:05,959
Sir, why is that man furious at you?
Have you mistreated anyone?

297
00:22:05,959 --> 00:22:09,562
We'll give a statement once we have
a full grasp of what happened here.

298
00:22:09,562 --> 00:22:11,431
Wait, where are you taking the mister?

299
00:22:11,431 --> 00:22:13,433
- Come on, son. Let's go home.
- Wait!

300
00:22:13,433 --> 00:22:14,734
Mom, where are we going?

301
00:22:14,734 --> 00:22:16,636
Home. Let's go home for now.

302
00:22:16,636 --> 00:22:18,938
He's safer in the office, Ma'am Tess.

303
00:22:18,938 --> 00:22:22,741
- Let's stay there for now.
- Come on. Let's go, son.

304
00:22:25,477 --> 00:22:27,869
Liam, how are you? Are you okay?

305
00:22:27,869 --> 00:22:30,283
"How are you", my foot!

306
00:22:30,283 --> 00:22:32,785
You were the first to leave
when everything got crazy.

307
00:22:32,785 --> 00:22:34,954
My God... I almost lost my son!

308
00:22:34,954 --> 00:22:36,990
And the only thing you can say is,
"how are you"?

309
00:22:36,990 --> 00:22:38,050
Mom...

310
00:22:38,050 --> 00:22:43,263
If something happens to my son,
Danilo, I'm telling you.

311
00:22:43,263 --> 00:22:45,498
You won't be able to handle me.

312
00:22:45,498 --> 00:22:48,768
Ma'am Tess, it's a protocol
to first keep the CEO secured

313
00:22:48,768 --> 00:22:50,470
during mishaps like the one earlier.

314
00:22:50,470 --> 00:22:55,275
No, I can feel
that Danilo is doing something shady,

315
00:22:55,275 --> 00:22:57,552
and my son is getting dragged into it.

316
00:22:57,552 --> 00:22:59,178
Mom...

317
00:22:59,178 --> 00:23:02,115
Oh, please, Tess.
Let me talk to my son first.

318
00:23:02,115 --> 00:23:04,450
Oh, so he's your son now.

319
00:23:04,450 --> 00:23:07,954
- But earlier, you...
- Mom, Mom, I'm okay.

320
00:23:07,954 --> 00:23:11,858
It's okay. Dad, I'm okay.

321
00:23:11,858 --> 00:23:13,660
I'm glad to hear that.

322
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:17,163
I had that old man investigated.

323
00:23:17,163 --> 00:23:20,133
He needs to pay for what he did.

324
00:23:20,133 --> 00:23:22,302
Are you going to send him to jail?

325
00:23:22,302 --> 00:23:23,903
Of course!

326
00:23:23,903 --> 00:23:26,472
He came with the intent to kill.

327
00:23:26,472 --> 00:23:28,174
That's attempted murder.

328
00:23:28,174 --> 00:23:30,009
But Dad, from what he said,

329
00:23:30,009 --> 00:23:32,645
it looked like I was the one
who did them wrong.

330
00:23:32,645 --> 00:23:34,714
What do you want to happen?

331
00:23:34,714 --> 00:23:37,417
I want to know why he did that to me.

332
00:23:37,417 --> 00:23:39,585
I want to talk to him.

333
00:23:39,585 --> 00:23:42,088
Liam, I forbid you to do that.

334
00:23:42,088 --> 00:23:45,692
He's probably not alone.

335
00:23:45,692 --> 00:23:47,994
You can't get into trouble.

336
00:23:47,994 --> 00:23:51,331
Tomorrow is the most important event
for our company,

337
00:23:51,331 --> 00:23:53,599
for our company's future.

338
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:56,769
What's happening tomorrow?

339
00:23:56,769 --> 00:24:00,013
Are you kidding me,
or are you trying to piss me off?

340
00:24:00,013 --> 00:24:03,343
See? The truth finally comes out.

341
00:24:03,343 --> 00:24:05,011
Right, Danilo?

342
00:24:05,011 --> 00:24:08,881
Your work and your company
are more important to you.

343
00:24:08,881 --> 00:24:12,818
Can't you be a father just this once, Danilo?

344
00:24:17,969 --> 00:24:22,372
You and your mom should go home.

345
00:24:23,262 --> 00:24:25,732
We better go home so you can get some rest.

346
00:24:25,732 --> 00:24:28,935
You might get involved in
your father's illegal dealings.

347
00:24:28,935 --> 00:24:30,737
Let's go.

348
00:24:30,737 --> 00:24:34,874
Come on, Tess.
Are you blaming me for this, too?

349
00:24:34,874 --> 00:24:38,945
Don't start with me, Danilo.
You won't be able to handle me.

350
00:24:38,945 --> 00:24:40,913
That's enough.

351
00:24:40,913 --> 00:24:42,464
Let's go.

352
00:24:43,687 --> 00:24:47,156
I'll send security to watch over you.

353
00:24:54,361 --> 00:24:56,063
Keep an eye on Liam.

354
00:24:56,063 --> 00:24:59,366
He's stubborn.
He might leave to see that old man.

355
00:24:59,366 --> 00:25:00,985
Go on.

356
00:25:13,013 --> 00:25:17,183
Your father isn't useless after all.

357
00:25:18,051 --> 00:25:21,921
Son, we're still not sure about your safety.

358
00:25:22,556 --> 00:25:30,196
What's the important event
that you need to attend tomorrow?

359
00:25:30,964 --> 00:25:32,799
Well, tomorrow we will have

360
00:25:32,799 --> 00:25:37,237
the investors' conference
of Casa Fuerte Properties.

361
00:25:37,237 --> 00:25:39,074
That's why the Señor said

362
00:25:39,074 --> 00:25:42,942
that tomorrow's event is really important
for the future of our company.

363
00:25:43,744 --> 00:25:45,234
To show investors

364
00:25:45,234 --> 00:25:50,032
that Casa Fuerte is
on solid financial footing.

365
00:25:50,033 --> 00:25:52,867
There are fears with the looming recession

366
00:25:52,868 --> 00:25:56,423
that the real estate sector
will become vulnerable.

367
00:25:56,423 --> 00:26:01,227
But since we are proceeding
with a mega development project,

368
00:26:01,228 --> 00:26:05,431
this can definitely boost
investors' confidence.

369
00:26:07,334 --> 00:26:09,702
Would you like some coffee?

370
00:26:13,472 --> 00:26:15,609
I'll go to sleep now.

371
00:26:15,609 --> 00:26:18,411
I've said a lot, but nobody seems to listen.

372
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:22,449
But you're right, Boss Bro.

373
00:26:22,449 --> 00:26:25,986
Go to sleep
so you will be well-rested tomorrow.

374
00:26:25,986 --> 00:26:28,822
But, Ma'am, can I charge my laptop here?

375
00:26:28,822 --> 00:26:31,758
I'll just check Boss Bro's speech
for tomorrow.

376
00:26:31,758 --> 00:26:33,926
Of course.

377
00:26:34,694 --> 00:26:36,496
Go on, son. Go to bed now.

378
00:26:36,496 --> 00:26:37,497
Get some rest.

379
00:26:37,497 --> 00:26:39,366
Okay. Good night, Mom.

380
00:26:39,366 --> 00:26:42,235
- Borj.
- Rest well, Boss Bro.

381
00:26:49,509 --> 00:26:51,978
Ma'am, the... Ma'am, the coffee.

382
00:26:51,978 --> 00:26:53,367
The coffee.

383
00:26:53,367 --> 00:26:54,514
Oh, yeah.

384
00:26:54,514 --> 00:26:55,515
- Coffee.
- Coffee.

385
00:26:55,515 --> 00:26:57,717
Yeah, for a while.

386
00:26:57,717 --> 00:26:59,652
Wait here.

387
00:27:36,823 --> 00:27:38,314
What's that?

388
00:27:42,629 --> 00:27:44,220
What's that?

389
00:28:07,919 --> 00:28:09,521
<i>Sorry, Mom.</i>

390
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:11,790
<i>I don't want you to worry.</i>

391
00:28:11,790 --> 00:28:15,927
<i>With all of the things I don't understand
in this reality...</i>

392
00:28:15,927 --> 00:28:17,795
<i>this one suddenly comes into the picture.</i>

393
00:28:21,633 --> 00:28:26,972
Is there any news about the identity
of the old man who attacked Liam?

394
00:28:26,972 --> 00:28:31,309
My assistants are still finding out
who that elder is.

395
00:28:31,309 --> 00:28:33,611
I'm still waiting for their reply.

396
00:28:34,683 --> 00:28:38,519
I still haven't heard from Señor Danilo.

397
00:28:39,317 --> 00:28:41,553
Your Señor? Oh, boy.

398
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:43,569
I don't trust him.

399
00:28:44,990 --> 00:28:49,494
I'm sure he's hiding something.

400
00:28:49,494 --> 00:28:53,532
He's the biggest swindler and liar I know.

401
00:28:53,532 --> 00:28:57,268
Ma'am, speaking from experience?

402
00:28:59,705 --> 00:29:03,174
What matters is that Liam is safe.

403
00:29:04,538 --> 00:29:07,979
That man. I'm worried about him.

404
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:17,334
[National Police]
[Sto. Cristo Police District]

405
00:29:19,826 --> 00:29:20,871
Chief...

406
00:29:20,871 --> 00:29:22,900
Sir, why are you here?

407
00:29:22,901 --> 00:29:26,233
Your father forbade you to come here.

408
00:29:26,234 --> 00:29:28,266
That old man might not be alone.

409
00:29:28,267 --> 00:29:30,301
You might get hurt.

410
00:29:30,301 --> 00:29:32,970
Sir, don't worry about me.

411
00:29:32,970 --> 00:29:35,438
I just want to talk to him.

412
00:29:38,809 --> 00:29:40,010
Nestor!

413
00:29:40,010 --> 00:29:41,362
Sir.

414
00:29:50,387 --> 00:29:54,858
Now... I got your attention.

415
00:29:57,161 --> 00:29:58,996
Mister...

416
00:29:58,996 --> 00:30:02,273
I came here
to get a full grasp of everything.

417
00:30:03,734 --> 00:30:06,737
Why did you do that to me?
I really can't remember anything.

418
00:30:06,737 --> 00:30:09,506
Stop lying.

419
00:30:09,506 --> 00:30:12,442
You can't fool us anymore.

420
00:30:13,143 --> 00:30:19,383
I may be old,
but I don't forget the evil things you did,

421
00:30:19,383 --> 00:30:21,218
especially you.

422
00:30:21,218 --> 00:30:22,553
Mister, I'm telling the truth.

423
00:30:22,553 --> 00:30:26,357
I really don't understand anything
from what you're saying.

424
00:30:26,357 --> 00:30:32,329
You dazzled us with money
that turned out to be measly after all.

425
00:30:32,329 --> 00:30:35,532
After you earned our trust,

426
00:30:35,532 --> 00:30:38,903
you didn't keep your end of the bargain.

427
00:30:38,903 --> 00:30:43,574
You tore down almost half of our neighborhood

428
00:30:43,574 --> 00:30:47,544
and stole our means of living.

429
00:30:47,544 --> 00:30:52,716
I won't let you fool and oppress us again!

430
00:30:52,716 --> 00:30:56,653
That's the truth!

431
00:31:05,763 --> 00:31:07,457
- Ma'am Tess.
- Yes?

432
00:31:07,457 --> 00:31:09,967
Here, I got an e-mail.

433
00:31:14,441 --> 00:31:17,207
Nestor Bartolome.

434
00:31:17,207 --> 00:31:20,410
A resident of Verde Village.

435
00:31:22,445 --> 00:31:27,949
The community
beside Casa Fuerte's Strongland Residences.

436
00:31:31,792 --> 00:31:33,960
Strongland Residences...

437
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:36,363
Isn't that Liam's latest project?

438
00:31:36,363 --> 00:31:37,913
Yes.

439
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:45,032
[Verde Village, Before]

440
00:31:45,033 --> 00:31:50,000
[Verde Village, After]

441
00:31:56,750 --> 00:32:00,487
I don't care if I rot in jail.

442
00:32:00,487 --> 00:32:05,038
You have to pay for all your wrongdoings.

443
00:32:06,159 --> 00:32:09,463
The law may be on your side,

444
00:32:09,463 --> 00:32:13,378
but you will deal with the law of the poor.

445
00:32:17,137 --> 00:32:18,772
Grandfather?

446
00:32:18,772 --> 00:32:20,394
My grandchild.

447
00:32:28,148 --> 00:32:29,949
Boss...

448
00:32:30,817 --> 00:32:33,085
I'm begging you.

449
00:32:34,121 --> 00:32:37,056
My grandfather is a good person.

450
00:32:38,356 --> 00:32:39,366
He only did that

451
00:32:39,367 --> 00:32:44,431
because of his love
for us and the people of Verde Village.

452
00:32:44,431 --> 00:32:46,566
That's why...

453
00:32:52,939 --> 00:32:55,775
Boss, I'm begging you.

454
00:32:59,225 --> 00:33:01,114
Let my grandfather go.

455
00:33:01,114 --> 00:33:02,616
You can put me in jail instead.

456
00:33:02,616 --> 00:33:04,351
Put me in jail instead of him.

457
00:33:04,351 --> 00:33:06,353
Please. He's old.

458
00:33:06,353 --> 00:33:08,355
Something bad might happen to him.
Put me in jail instead.

459
00:33:08,355 --> 00:33:11,958
If you need to lock someone up, let it be me.

460
00:33:13,193 --> 00:33:15,127
Boss, please.

461
00:33:19,697 --> 00:33:21,301
I will do everything.

462
00:33:21,301 --> 00:33:23,837
If you really need to lock someone up,
let it be me.

463
00:33:23,837 --> 00:33:26,139
Let my grandfather go.

464
00:33:26,139 --> 00:33:29,175
You have to leave, Sir.
We don't want you to get in trouble.

465
00:33:30,211 --> 00:33:32,079
Boss.

466
00:33:33,847 --> 00:33:35,681
My grandchild.

467
00:33:45,225 --> 00:33:47,026
Liam.

468
00:33:49,196 --> 00:33:50,997
Mom.

469
00:33:50,997 --> 00:33:53,631
What has gotten into your head
that you came here?

470
00:33:53,631 --> 00:33:57,838
I came to understand everything.
But I only got more confused.

471
00:33:57,838 --> 00:33:59,940
Boss Bro...

472
00:33:59,940 --> 00:34:03,410
we already know why he ran amok.

473
00:34:23,630 --> 00:34:25,298
Son.

474
00:34:25,298 --> 00:34:29,135
Don't be impulsive.

475
00:34:29,135 --> 00:34:32,072
It's good I know
what's running through your head.

476
00:34:32,072 --> 00:34:36,175
I knew you were going to see that old man.

477
00:34:38,912 --> 00:34:40,713
Sorry, Mom.

478
00:34:44,303 --> 00:34:48,194
Mister Nestor told me
that I spoke with the residents.

479
00:34:49,623 --> 00:34:52,425
That's something you should remember
because you are...

480
00:34:52,425 --> 00:34:55,395
But Boss Bro...

481
00:34:55,395 --> 00:34:59,432
you meet a lot of people every day.

482
00:34:59,432 --> 00:35:02,102
So it's possible that you won't remember him,

483
00:35:02,102 --> 00:35:05,404
especially if you're focused on the project.

484
00:35:06,099 --> 00:35:08,860
But why are they furious at me?

485
00:35:09,843 --> 00:35:13,346
What did I do wrong?

486
00:35:13,346 --> 00:35:19,152
Son, only Danilo can answer our questions.

487
00:35:19,152 --> 00:35:22,211
Do you want me to talk to your dad?

488
00:35:25,625 --> 00:35:27,426
Hold on.

489
00:35:29,796 --> 00:35:32,131
Oh, son.

490
00:35:37,871 --> 00:35:39,614
He sent a message.

491
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:43,109
Danilo is in our house.

492
00:35:43,109 --> 00:35:47,079
The security already reported to him
that you went out.

493
00:35:48,281 --> 00:35:54,888
Mom, I don't want to see Dad
after what I discovered tonight.

494
00:35:54,888 --> 00:35:58,058
He might dictate again
how I should handle things.

495
00:35:58,058 --> 00:36:00,946
Where will we go, son?

496
00:36:11,567 --> 00:36:21,534
[Incoming call: Dad]

497
00:36:23,300 --> 00:36:34,266
[Incoming call: Dad]

498
00:36:34,267 --> 00:36:37,466
<i>What more plot twists should I expect?</i>

499
00:36:37,467 --> 00:36:40,900
<i>Universe, take it easy.</i>

500
00:36:46,873 --> 00:36:50,810
I'm glad you came here, Auntie.

501
00:36:52,212 --> 00:36:58,118
I told Liam that it might not be a good idea,
because it's already late.

502
00:36:58,118 --> 00:37:01,187
It's all right with me, Auntie.

503
00:37:01,187 --> 00:37:03,790
Love, I'm so sorry.

504
00:37:03,790 --> 00:37:07,761
I got so busy with work today.
I wasn't able to check on you.

505
00:37:07,761 --> 00:37:09,896
Are you really okay?

506
00:37:09,896 --> 00:37:11,531
Are you hurt? Did you get yourself checked?

507
00:37:11,531 --> 00:37:14,034
I'm okay, Via.

508
00:37:14,034 --> 00:37:17,336
I don't want you to worry about my troubles.

509
00:37:18,738 --> 00:37:21,307
Don't worry about you?

510
00:37:21,307 --> 00:37:23,576
Love, I'm your girlfriend.

511
00:37:23,576 --> 00:37:28,447
I worry the same way your mom does.

512
00:37:30,250 --> 00:37:33,620
Son, you're being impulsive.

513
00:37:33,620 --> 00:37:35,072
Mom.

514
00:37:39,793 --> 00:37:43,229
Where can I take a nap, Via?

515
00:37:43,229 --> 00:37:44,998
You can use the guest room, Auntie.

516
00:37:44,998 --> 00:37:46,599
- Over there?
- Yes.

517
00:37:46,599 --> 00:37:49,935
- Do you need help?
- No. Thank you.

518
00:38:06,753 --> 00:38:08,921
When you're stressed...

519
00:38:10,523 --> 00:38:14,159
this is the only thing
that makes you feel better.

520
00:38:21,468 --> 00:38:23,949
Aren't you turned off?

521
00:38:25,538 --> 00:38:29,575
You learned how ruthless I am
when it comes to business.

522
00:38:30,443 --> 00:38:32,411
No.

523
00:38:34,380 --> 00:38:40,486
One thing I know about you...

524
00:38:41,888 --> 00:38:44,891
is that when you do something bad,

525
00:38:44,891 --> 00:38:47,259
you do it for a good reason.

526
00:38:55,368 --> 00:39:00,373
Liam, you taught me

527
00:39:00,373 --> 00:39:03,813
that everyone can have a second chance.

528
00:39:05,912 --> 00:39:09,727
Just like how you gave me
my second chance at happiness.

529
00:39:20,326 --> 00:39:22,079
Thank you...

530
00:39:23,496 --> 00:39:25,946
for still believing in me.

531
00:40:05,534 --> 00:40:10,968
[Annual Investors Conference]

532
00:40:12,574 --> 00:40:17,738
Everyone, a warm applause
to the man of the hour.

533
00:40:20,887 --> 00:40:23,522
Our special guest...

534
00:40:24,891 --> 00:40:30,697
is the great and hard-working congressman,
Ramon dela Peña.

535
00:40:36,736 --> 00:40:39,672
Congressman, thank you very much
for gracing this occasion

536
00:40:39,672 --> 00:40:41,541
despite your very busy schedule.

537
00:40:41,541 --> 00:40:43,576
- Thank you, Sir.
- Thank you, thank you.

538
00:40:43,576 --> 00:40:48,413
With him is his beautiful daughter,
Victoria dela Peña.

539
00:40:59,726 --> 00:41:01,761
- Thank you, Danilo.
- Thank you, thank you.

540
00:41:01,761 --> 00:41:02,929
This is the engineer.

541
00:41:02,929 --> 00:41:04,230
Oh, engineer...

542
00:41:04,230 --> 00:41:06,699
- Love.
- Thank you...

543
00:41:06,699 --> 00:41:07,734
This is Engineer Diaz.

544
00:41:07,734 --> 00:41:10,937
Sorry I did not tell you I was coming.

545
00:41:10,937 --> 00:41:13,572
Dad suddenly asked me to come.

546
00:41:14,497 --> 00:41:16,609
It's okay.

547
00:41:16,609 --> 00:41:18,458
Boss Bro...

548
00:41:18,458 --> 00:41:22,607
I know lots of things
have been bothering you.

549
00:41:22,607 --> 00:41:24,183
So here.

550
00:41:24,183 --> 00:41:28,487
Just read it so we can be over and done with,
with the conference.

551
00:41:31,224 --> 00:41:33,059
Do the right thing.

552
00:41:33,059 --> 00:41:34,560
- Thank you, Danilo.
- Thank you.

553
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:36,995
Engineer Diaz, nice to meet you.

554
00:41:39,438 --> 00:41:41,773
We'll talk later.

555
00:41:43,770 --> 00:41:45,638
Sure, Dad...

556
00:41:45,638 --> 00:41:48,274
Right after my speech.

557
00:41:48,274 --> 00:41:50,576
Who said you are going to speak?

558
00:41:50,576 --> 00:41:52,678
I'll take care of it.

559
00:41:54,224 --> 00:41:58,117
Ladies and gentlemen,
let us all give a warm welcome

560
00:41:58,117 --> 00:42:01,631
to the man that we all call "Señor".

561
00:42:05,885 --> 00:42:07,557
Oh...

562
00:42:10,197 --> 00:42:11,000
Well, I guess

563
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:14,034
there has been some slight changes
to the program.

564
00:42:14,034 --> 00:42:17,771
So, ladies and gentlemen,
let us begin this conference.

565
00:42:17,771 --> 00:42:20,841
Engineer William Herrera.

566
00:42:44,531 --> 00:42:47,533
Thank you so much for that warm welcome.

567
00:42:48,535 --> 00:42:53,607
To my dad, the president of Herrera Group,

568
00:42:53,607 --> 00:42:56,709
Señor Danilo Herrera.

569
00:42:58,145 --> 00:43:00,981
To the Board of Directors...

570
00:43:00,981 --> 00:43:02,716
and to all of you here

571
00:43:02,716 --> 00:43:06,386
who share the vision of our organization...

572
00:43:06,386 --> 00:43:10,790
Welcome to this year's investors' conference.

573
00:43:12,292 --> 00:43:14,728
What is your son doing?

574
00:43:14,728 --> 00:43:17,097
I don't know, my friend.

575
00:43:17,097 --> 00:43:21,601
Let me begin by telling you...

576
00:43:21,601 --> 00:43:25,199
how exciting this year is for all of us.

577
00:43:27,974 --> 00:43:32,847
<i>A big change is coming for everyone.</i>

578
00:43:40,787 --> 00:43:42,158
Hey Nestor,

579
00:43:42,158 --> 00:43:45,092
looks like the man you wanted to stab
has a big company event.

580
00:43:45,092 --> 00:43:47,794
<i>Through the years,</i>

581
00:43:47,794 --> 00:43:51,264
<i>we have overlooked our values
as an organization.</i>

582
00:43:53,433 --> 00:43:55,568
<i>And that's wrong.</i>

583
00:43:57,371 --> 00:44:00,140
<i>Ours is not a perfect company,</i>

584
00:44:00,140 --> 00:44:06,479
<i>but that doesn't mean
we won't do things for the greater good.</i>

585
00:44:09,683 --> 00:44:12,518
It's not just for our own sake,

586
00:44:13,153 --> 00:44:18,625
but also for the lives of every community
we are supposed to serve.

587
00:44:18,625 --> 00:44:21,828
Because of our desire to make money,

588
00:44:21,828 --> 00:44:25,132
we forget about how to be human.

589
00:44:25,132 --> 00:44:27,066
And I don't think

590
00:44:27,067 --> 00:44:32,305
that is the sustainable way
to run this business.

591
00:44:33,157 --> 00:44:38,128
So tonight, I announce...

592
00:44:39,179 --> 00:44:43,733
that I will put on hold
all the development projects of Casa Fuerte

593
00:44:43,734 --> 00:44:46,070
for the time being.

594
00:44:50,857 --> 00:44:53,760
And I will hire an independent firm

595
00:44:53,760 --> 00:44:57,697
to assess the environmental impact
and effects of our projects.

596
00:44:57,697 --> 00:45:00,727
I think it's only right

597
00:45:00,727 --> 00:45:07,541
that we take it to heart
the real meaning of property development.

598
00:45:07,541 --> 00:45:09,375
Turn the mic off.

599
00:45:15,415 --> 00:45:20,453
A company that doesn't trample on anyone.

600
00:45:22,621 --> 00:45:26,859
A company that doesn't hurt anyone.

601
00:45:26,859 --> 00:45:29,094
I know that a lot of you will disagree.

602
00:45:29,094 --> 00:45:31,630
There will be setbacks.

603
00:45:31,630 --> 00:45:38,121
But I promise you,
that we will become a better company.

604
00:45:41,975 --> 00:45:43,976
Let's get out of here.

605
00:45:57,856 --> 00:45:59,257
What was that about?

606
00:45:59,257 --> 00:46:01,726
I'm just doing the right thing, Dad.

607
00:46:01,726 --> 00:46:03,595
Do you suddenly feel guilt?

608
00:46:03,595 --> 00:46:05,864
When will you do the right thing?

609
00:46:05,864 --> 00:46:10,602
Do you think I am the one
who calls the shots in Casa Fuerte?

610
00:46:10,602 --> 00:46:12,404
Are you not?

611
00:46:12,404 --> 00:46:16,207
I thought this is a chance
for us to get along.

612
00:46:16,207 --> 00:46:18,209
But what have you done?

613
00:46:18,209 --> 00:46:19,911
You turned me into the bad guy!

614
00:46:19,911 --> 00:46:21,946
Are you a fool?

615
00:46:21,946 --> 00:46:24,249
Did you hit your head somewhere?

616
00:46:24,249 --> 00:46:26,117
Have you forgotten?

617
00:46:26,117 --> 00:46:29,287
Everything we do in Casa Fuerte is your idea!

618
00:46:29,287 --> 00:46:32,490
We are successful because of you.

619
00:46:32,490 --> 00:46:36,327
I may love money, but you are greedy!

620
00:46:36,327 --> 00:46:37,996
That's a lie!

621
00:46:37,996 --> 00:46:40,464
None of what you said is true!

622
00:46:41,933 --> 00:46:43,450
Liam!

623
00:47:07,067 --> 00:47:12,433
[Antique Typewriter for sale]

624
00:47:12,434 --> 00:47:14,968
[Second-hand sale]
[Online Shop for secondhand items]

625
00:47:24,874 --> 00:47:27,166
Son...

626
00:47:27,167 --> 00:47:29,434
[Trade-ins.net, Typewriters]
Time to eat.

627
00:47:45,263 --> 00:47:47,464
My son...

628
00:47:50,034 --> 00:47:52,136
Liam...

629
00:48:20,632 --> 00:48:23,334
I went to your office,
but they said you weren't there.

630
00:48:24,969 --> 00:48:29,540
I need an update
on the environmental clearances I asked for.

631
00:48:33,778 --> 00:48:35,746
Didn't you hear me?

632
00:48:36,614 --> 00:48:40,218
No one is taking care of the clearances.

633
00:48:40,218 --> 00:48:43,755
It's business as usual again in Casa Fuerte.

634
00:48:43,755 --> 00:48:49,727
None of the investors and directors
believe in your vision.

635
00:48:49,727 --> 00:48:51,283
What do you mean?

636
00:48:53,099 --> 00:48:56,035
What's so difficult to understand
in what I said?

637
00:48:59,404 --> 00:49:02,607
You revealed everything
that's happening in Casa Fuerte

638
00:49:02,607 --> 00:49:06,410
because of what you did at the conference.

639
00:49:07,946 --> 00:49:10,515
So, as of today...

640
00:49:10,515 --> 00:49:13,884
you're no longer the president of Casa Fuerte.

641
00:49:15,854 --> 00:49:17,455
I can do it, Dad.

642
00:49:17,455 --> 00:49:19,958
I can make us better.

643
00:49:19,958 --> 00:49:22,193
We don't need to become evil.

644
00:49:22,193 --> 00:49:25,363
I said, you're done with Casa Fuerte!

645
00:49:25,363 --> 00:49:27,831
You've done enough damage!

646
00:49:56,728 --> 00:50:02,966
<i>We do unthinkable things
because of intense feelings of love.</i>

647
00:50:03,668 --> 00:50:07,572
<i>You tore down
almost half of our neighborhood.</i>

648
00:50:07,572 --> 00:50:10,675
<i>And you stole our livelihood.</i>

649
00:50:10,675 --> 00:50:12,267
<i>Please, don't throw my grandfather
behind bars.</i>

650
00:50:12,267 --> 00:50:13,811
<i>Lock me up instead.</i>

651
00:50:13,811 --> 00:50:16,167
<i>Let it be me.</i>

652
00:50:16,167 --> 00:50:18,115
<i>Mom...</i>

653
00:50:20,685 --> 00:50:23,021
<i>Mom...</i>

654
00:50:23,021 --> 00:50:28,358
<i>You taught me
that everyone deserves a second chance.</i>

655
00:50:44,042 --> 00:50:46,210
<i>This time...</i>

656
00:50:46,210 --> 00:50:51,382
<i>showing your weakness is not cowardice.</i>

657
00:50:51,382 --> 00:50:56,661
<i>I thought everything would be better
if you were here.</i>

658
00:51:08,066 --> 00:51:10,101
So, I'm giving you a second chance, Liam.

659
00:51:10,101 --> 00:51:11,602
Are you putting me back to Casa Fuerte?

660
00:51:11,602 --> 00:51:14,572
No. But I will put you in another company.

661
00:51:14,572 --> 00:51:16,140
In Blacksmith Productions.

662
00:51:16,140 --> 00:51:18,309
Isn't that Vergil's production house?

663
00:51:18,309 --> 00:51:19,577
Who would have thought?

664
00:51:19,577 --> 00:51:23,247
Casa Fuerte's wonder boy,
Herrera's prodigal son,

665
00:51:23,247 --> 00:51:24,749
ended up in my company.

666
00:51:24,749 --> 00:51:28,252
Of all people who look at that billboard,

667
00:51:28,252 --> 00:51:30,655
you're the only one who's sad.

668
00:51:30,655 --> 00:51:34,759
Well, maybe that's how it goes. Right, Bro?

669
00:51:34,759 --> 00:51:39,062
She's up there and you're down here.

670
00:51:39,731 --> 00:51:41,666
Is everything set?
Have you checked everything?

671
00:51:41,666 --> 00:51:43,067
Yes, Miss Via.

672
00:51:43,067 --> 00:51:46,404
Our vlog interview for today
is just a mini challenge.

673
00:51:46,404 --> 00:51:50,374
Speaking of, our guest is already here.
